---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { href } from '../../lib/href';
import Widget from '../../components/VirtualZeroReference.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="The Virtual Zero Reference — ECE/ME 732">
  <p class="crumb"><a href={href("/interactives/")}>← Interactives</a></p>
  <h1>The Virtual Zero Reference</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    A proportional current loop never quite reaches its command, and turning
    the gain up only narrows the gap. The reason is that the winding
    resistance is a feedback gain too, and it regulates toward a command of
    zero. Two references pull on one current and it settles between them.
    Decouple the resistance and the second reference is gone, with no
    integrator in the controller.
  </p>
  <Widget />
</BaseLayout>
